{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"Nexus()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses it. Choose ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"reference"},{"text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"The sparse-set storage","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The archetype storage","anchor":"The-archetype-storage","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html"},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" drops all tables.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What the numbers say","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":", see "},{"code":"Benchmarks\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Case","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sparse set","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Archetype"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"23 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"6.1 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1 800 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 180 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4 900 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1 730 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}]}]]],"alignments":["left","right","right"],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two (","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyOneComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating with ","type":"text"},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick","level":3,"text":"Which storage to pick","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe","level":3,"text":"Differences you can observe","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Family spans.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents"},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"text":", and know what changes.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage","roleHeading":"Article"},"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of events a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" subscribes to."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventMask"}],"title":"NexusEventMask","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","abstract":[{"text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Entity/identifier":{"abstract":[{"text":"The unique entity identifier.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/entity\/identifier","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"identifier","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS16EntityIdentifierV","text":"EntityIdentifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"abstract":[{"text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"FirebladeECS"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/default":{"abstract":[{"text":"The storage ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)"},{"text":" uses by default: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/default","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"default","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"`default`"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"NexusEventDelegate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/archetype":{"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.archetype","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/archetype","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"archetype"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"One table per component set, a column per component type in every table, an index from entity to table and row.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"topic","title":"Which storage to pick","abstract":[],"kind":"section","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#Which-storage-to-pick"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Clears all data from the Nexus.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"clear()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clear"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(writing:_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MutableSpan","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" write access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableSpan"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(writing:_:)","title":"componentSpan(writing:_:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComponents":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read a copy, replace a component or change it in place."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/readingandwritingcomponents","title":"Reading and writing components","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","kind":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say","title":"What the numbers say","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"componentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reading","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"